## The Clockmaker's Package
aspect: us-comic
author: lazycomics test suite
genre: steampunk noir
description: Held-out script for tools/golden_run.py --story and tools/refiner_bench.py. A different cast, setting and style from story.cbml, so prompt and generation changes are checked beyond the story they were tuned on.

PAGE preset:grid-2x2

PANEL A
loc: STEAMPUNK_ALLEY
chars: NOVA, REX, MARLO
shot: medium shot under a flickering gas lamp
mood: tense
> Nova and Rex corner Marlo against a brick wall.
NOVA: "Where is the package, Marlo?"
MARLO: "I swear I never opened it."
REX: ~He is lying.~

PANEL B
loc: STEAMPUNK_ALLEY
chars: REX
shot: low angle
mood: ominous
> Rex stands at the heavy iron door of the clock workshop.
[sfx pos:top-right color:#cc8800] KNOCK KNOCK

PANEL C
loc: STEAMPUNK_ALLEY
chars: NOVA, REX
shot: over-the-shoulder two-shot
mood: grim
> Nova unfolds a crumpled letter while Rex looks over her shoulder.
NOVA: "It has the clockmaker's seal on it."
REX: "Then we know who sent it."

PANEL D
loc: CLOCK_WORKSHOP
chars: MARLO
shot: close-up
mood: panicked
> Marlo backs away from the workbench, hands raised.
MARLO: !"It was not my fault!"!

PAGE preset:wide-top

PANEL A
loc: STEAMPUNK_ALLEY
chars: NOVA, REX, MARLO
shot: wide shot down the length of the alley
mood: hurried
> The three of them hurry through the alley as steam vents burst around them.
[caption bg:#101010 color:#e0d0a0 pos:top-left] Midnight.
[sfx pos:bottom-right color:#888888] HISSSS

PANEL B
loc: CLOCK_WORKSHOP
chars: NOVA
shot: medium shot
mood: uneasy
> Nova scans the walls of ticking clocks.
NOVA: ~Too many clocks.~

PANEL C
loc: CLOCK_WORKSHOP
chars: REX, MARLO, NOVA
shot: medium group shot
mood: tense standoff
> Rex blocks the workshop door while Marlo edges toward the back and Nova watches them both.
[sfx pos:top-center color:#cc8800] TICK TOCK
REX: "Nobody leaves until the clocks stop."
MARLO: "They never stop."
